# Drive — compose epic → publish → auto-all → review → local cleanup

`/iflow-drive <N>` takes an existing GitHub issue and runs: draft epic
(auto-accept unless grill-me) → publish every stage → `/iflow-auto` each
epoch (yolo **and** non-yolo issues) → final review (create leftover
findings) → local cleanup (`-d` reachable + `-D` squash-landed) →
`/iflow-status`.

See `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ designs_folder }}/drive-mode.md`.

{% include "skills/_model_directive.md.j2" %}

{% include "skills/_resolve_project_root.md.j2" %}

## Input

- **`<N>`** — existing issue that becomes the epic anchor (required).
- **`grill` / `grill-me`** — interview the epic goal before draft-accept.
- **`loops:<n>`** — forwarded to `/iflow-auto`.
- **`nonyolo:merge|pr-only|stop`** — how `yolo: no` issues land
  (forwarded to `/iflow-auto` → `/iflow-cycle`; default from config
  **`{{ cycle_nonyolo }}`**). A `yolo: no` judgment is not a stop by itself.
- **`dry-run`** — report only (stages, queue, non-yolo issues, cleanup
  plan); no confirm / no writes.
- Mid-run **`abort` / `stop` / `cancel` / `halt`** — stop at the next
  stage or issue boundary (`drive_status.md` → `aborted`).

## Steps

Follow `{{ agent_dir }}/skills/iflow-drive/SKILL.md` verbatim.

## Constraints

- Off-path; never auto-dispatched by `/iflow`.
- One confirm covers draft-accept, publish-all, auto-all (both lanes),
  final-review creates, and the local cleanup (`-d` **and** `-D`). Do not
  re-ask those.
- Auto's budget ask (accept / grant N more loops / abort) stays a
  planned pause.
- Never rebase / force-push / push the **default branch**. Issue branches
  may be rebased by `agent sync-branch` (optionally `--base <parent>`)
  and pushed `--force-with-lease` — that is normal PR-queue sync.
- Cleanup is `local only`: `-d` on reachable, `-D` on squash-landed (and
  merged-PR-divergent with nothing newer than the merge), never
  `unique_work`, never Phase B. Report tip SHAs of `-D` deletions.
- "Already merged" on a merge attempt is a success, not a stop.
- Commit `Published:` lines off default (#303).
